Valkyries seemed easy, so I tried a wizard.  It was a bit exciting
before I got Magicbane, but after that, it seemed a piece of cake.

The wiki says that the knight is perhaps the easiest class in the
game, so I tried that next.  First knight had 44 hp before finding a
giant mimic.  Engraved Elbereth.  looked down, read Elbereth.  and
then the Giant mimic hits! The giant mimic hits!  I guess looking down
smudged the word.  dang.  Engrave again.  Look again.  oops, didn't
write correctly this time.  The giant mimic hits! The giant mimic
hits!  DYWYPI?

The next knight did well and had most of an ascension kit ready.  I
was hoping to get some silver dragon scales to enchant, so I could
take off my GDSM and give my "oR to my pet.  Despite polypiling, I
hadn't found a single ?oGenocide, though, so Lichs were still roaming
around.  I was in Baalzebub's lair and decided to use a rubber chicken
to take out an L.  and then I was going to use it to take out
Baalzebub.  until I fell into a pit.  DYWYPI?

Now it's a new moon, which I'm sure isn't helping things.  I hit a
magic trap.  tried to engrave Elbereth while blind (despite having a
carrot in inventory).  and then all in 1 turn:  It hits! It hits! It
bits! It bites! It bites! It misses. It hits! It hits! DYWYPI?

The next knight found a vampire bat.  It successfully bites.  The bite
was poisoned.  You feel weaker!  Your movements are slowed.  It bites
4 times in a row.  Let me try to jump to the nearby stairs...  You are
carrying too much to jump.  It bites 4 times in a row.  DYWYPI?

My next level 3 knight finds a little dog on DL3.  The dog is getting
the better of me, so I figured I'd try to pray for HP.  Only I prayed
with 6HP out of 33.  I didn't realize that the prayer didn't do diddly
until DYWYPI?

The level 6 knight was doing okay.  found an uncursed magic lamp,
which I figured I'd save until I could bless it.  a lone fire ant
shows up in Minetown.  gee, I'd like a chance at getting fire
resistance... Wow, the ant did 10HP damage to me in one turn.  Wow,
the ant did 15HP damage to me in the next turn.  I'll hit it one more
time to see if I can kill it before I zap it with my /oTele.  Wow, the
ant just did 20+HP damage to me.  DYWYPI?

Okay, so I clearly made several mistakes.  I guess I'll never move
another step while wielding a rubber chicken.  Jumping while burdened
was obvioulsy n00b.  and I'll be more careful around fire ants when
not fire resistant.

My current knight seems to be doing okay riding an adult horse with a
BoH in minetown, and should be able to buy 1 or 2 layers of protection
after a bit of credit cloning.

but knights are certainly not seeming easy.  The saddled pony thing is
nice.  but you can't ride for a few XLs.  The +1 lance is nice for
pounding.  but you don't want to joust before you can get your luck
up, and you can't get a luckstone for a long time.  Jumping is
somewhat useful for escape, but the knight's jump doesn't get you that
far away.  A ton of your starting attribute points are spent on
charisma, which makes credit cloning faster, but isn't nearly as
useful as St, Co, or Dx.  (According to my simulations, knights
actually have the worst starting Co and Dx).  The human restriction
doesn't help, either.

I'm not trying to argue that knights are a hard class.  but "the
easiest class in the game"?  really?


